# The device calls (tests/programs/devices.asm): tones measured by the
# kernel's probe, a rest, the game port (DOSBox-X emulates a centred stick),
# the mouse's reset answered through IRQ4, a byte to the modem on COM4 (to
# no one: MAME's AT has no COM4, the others no peer here), and SYS_WAIT.
program: devices
define: TEST_SOUND
timeout: 60
---
rx286, test build
probe: the speaker sounds at the frequency asked
sound: 440 Hz: no error
probe: the speaker sounds at the frequency asked
sound: 1000 Hz: no error
probe: the speaker sounds at the frequency asked
sound: 2000 Hz: no error
sound: a rest of 5 ticks: 5 ticks
sound: 18 Hz: error 3
sound: 20001 Hz: error 3
sound: 501 ticks: error 3
@bochs joystick: buttons 00, axes absent absent absent absent
@dosbox-x joystick: buttons 00, axes present present absent absent
@mame joystick: buttons 00, axes absent absent absent absent
mouse: present, at 320, 100, buttons 0
serial: write: no error
serial: read: no error
wait: 5 ticks: slept, events 00
wait: a key, 3 ticks at most: events 00
wait: nothing for ever: error 3
wait: an unknown event: error 3
wait: registers kept
